# Contracts package

`packages/contracts` is the single source of truth for API shapes shared by
`apps/api` and `src/`. Both sides import from `@interwjuer/contracts` — never
duplicate or redefine these types locally in either app.

- Plain TypeScript types/enums only — no Prisma types, no framework types
  (no Hono `Context`, no React types).
- One file per domain concept (e.g. `job-applications.ts`,
  `job-application-mutations.ts`, `enums.ts`), re-exported from `index.ts`.
- Request/response DTOs are separate from Prisma models — only include fields
  the API actually returns or accepts, not the raw table shape.
- Changing a contract is step 1 of any cross-layer feature (see
  `architecture-boundaries.mdc` feature order) — update it before touching
  Application/Infrastructure/Presentation/Frontend.
